ks ago  and definitely brings a  whole entire aspect to what spider-man 3  could be for example when the morbius  trailer dropped we all saw that  spider-man existed within his universe  and then at the end of the trailer we  saw adrian tombs  aka vulture from spider-man far from  home  two different universes well doctor  strange is a character who does have the  ability to open up  portals to different universes meaning  that if somebody  say a villain found their way into our  main universe doctor strange would be  the one to know how to get them to go  back or defeat them  it is confirmed that doctor strange is  going to be taking on the mentor role of  peter parker  peter has basically had a mentor each  film in the first film he had tony stark  and the second one he  kind of had nick fury of course it was  actually talos  but he was there for him and of course  so was happy  and now the mentor in spider-man 3 will  be doctor strange  and speaking of doctor strange's role  and different universes it has been  confirmed that jamie foxx is going to be  reprising his role as  electro now of course we saw jamie foxx  playing elektro in the amazing  spider-man number two  and there's actually been kind of  conflicting rumors about his role  some reports have said that jamie foxx's  elektra was going to be an entirely  new electro and not from the amazing  spider-man universe  however when the announcement was made  that jamie foxx would be joining the  next spider-man film  as electro he posted to his instagram  confirming that he was indeed going to  be in the next film  and on the instagram post he put a  picture of spider-man  into the spider-verse now there's really  no reason for him to post a picture of  the spider-verse unless the spider-verse  actually  has something to do with his return and  also why would they have jaime fox play  electro again  if he was going to be a different  electro why not just get a different  actor  because after all that is kind 